  "derivation": "The bijection seam equation equates the two branch boundary values. The exponential boundary 2^(-k-2) is positive, so -log_2(k+2)-2>0. With k+2>0 this gives log_2(k+2)<-2, hence 0<k+2<1/4 and -2<k<-7/4<-1. Therefore -k>7/4>1, so each allowed integer a=-2,-1,0,1 lies below -k.",
